[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176762522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4176762522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4176762522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc749Faa","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T11:23:20Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T11:23:36Z","body":"The fuzzy match algorithm was tweaked numerous times. There is always some problem and \"fixes\" tend to make it worse in some unpredicted edge cases (that turn out to be common).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176762522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4177911935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4177911935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4177911935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75BeB_","user":{"login":"michaelgundlach","id":5141333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDEzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5141333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelgundlach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T13:33:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T13:33:40Z","body":"> It makes sense \r\n> I would expect player.tscn to be selected in the above example, no?\r\n\r\nNo actually, both of the search results have the same path length! I agree that case should be addressed, but I didn't want to do too much in one PR. If this PR is accepted I'm happy to do some work on other weird behaviors like these.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4177911935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4178817424","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4178817424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4178817424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75E7GQ","user":{"login":"michaelgundlach","id":5141333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDEzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5141333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelgundlach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T15:50:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T15:50:50Z","body":"To clarify: both the base branch and this PR show the same behavior that @AdriaandeJongh sees, as they are both exact matches, in the filename, on two word boundaries, on paths of identical length.  This PR does not affect that case.\r\n\r\nThis PR addresses the unpleasant situation where the user has\r\n```\r\nres://entities/main/player.tscn\r\nres://dead_player.tscn\r\n```\r\nand wants to select `player.tscn`.  They are thinking of the filename `player.tscn`, they start to type `playe`, and they get\r\n```\r\nres://dead_[playe]r.tscn\r\nres://entities/main/[playe]r.tscn\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is unpleasant for multiple reasons, but the biggest is that there is no obvious<sup>1</sup> way for the user to course correct to prioritize when they see this happen, without starting over.  They could, in frustration, continue to type the full name of the desired file, `player.tscn`, and they'd just get\r\n```\r\nres://dead_[player.tscn]\r\nres://entities/main/[player.tscn]\r\n```\r\n\r\nTyping the beginning of a filename is a strong indicator to the system that the user wants that filename, since (at least English-speaking) users tend to think of filenames by what they start with, rather than a word in the middle of the file.  This PR just says \"if the user types the beginning of a filename, they almost certainly want that file.\"\r\n\r\n<sup>[1] In writing this PR I discovered that the system allows space-separated tokens and allows them out of order, so the user could in fact course correct by typing `playe main`.  But this is not obvious.</sup>","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4178817424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4180341007","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4180341007","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4180341007,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75KvEP","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T20:35:21Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T20:35:21Z","body":"> I'm not 100% convinced by the idea of doing small incremental modification and think it should be reworked to have a better system then a score system (similar maybe to the one for autocompletion) and enumerate all the common problem to find a solution that would satisfy all condition.\r\n\r\nI mean, #98278 was supposed to do that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4180341007/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4246101444","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4246101444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4246101444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79Fl3E","user":{"login":"michaelgundlach","id":5141333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDEzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5141333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelgundlach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T18:06:21Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T18:06:21Z","body":"I've looked deeper into this, and I'm fine doing @ajreckof's version (\"+4 for filename start\") vs mine (\"+4 for filename start in exact token matches.\")\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe algo as written **already** perversely awards breaking inexact search terms up, to stuff the suffix into the filename for a bonus.  E.g. a search for `mainmenu` has `/[main]/[menu]/data.gd` losing to `/[main]/da[m]age/all_[enu]ms.gd` because `enu` gets a 3*3 point bonus for being in the filename.  \r\n\r\n@ajreckof's version does make that perverse behavior a little more likely, but not much.  Here are several more (very contrived!) examples where my code and the original code do the right thing, but @ajreckof's tips the scales the wrong way.\r\n\r\n|Search token|My and original code's preference |ajreckof's version's preference|\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n|`//steam` | `./meta/steam/keys.gd` | `./old/useless/team_data.tres` |\r\n|`/sprites.gd` | `./sprites/all.gd` | `./spells/rites_and_hexes.gd` |\r\n| `/surfaces` | `./building/ext_surfaces/detail.gd` | `./bomb/the_survivors/faces.tscn` |\r\n| `main_hostiles` | `./main_game/hostiles/data.gd` | `./main_game/hospice/tileset.png` |\r\n|`cache_debug` | `./cache/main_debug.gd` | `./control_data/checkbox_debug.gd` |\r\n\r\nBut since there are plenty of examples where all 3 versions of the code give the wrong result, I don't think it's a big deal.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe deeper fix would be to not give the existing large bonus to token substrings found in the filename, unless they started on a word boundary _within the search token itself_.\r\n\r\nE.g. a search for `/surfaces` wouldn't get a bonus for finding `faces` in the filename, but a search for `main_faces` would, because `faces` is preceded by a word boundary character `_`.\r\n\r\n### tl;dr\r\n\r\n\r\n@ajreckof's version doesn't handle the perverse cases much worse than mine or the original algorithm, and it does address his `menu__debug` example whereas my version doesn't.  So I'll update to use his version.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4246101444/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4246551249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4246551249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4246551249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79HTrR","user":{"login":"michaelgundlach","id":5141333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDEzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5141333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelgundlach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T19:23:01Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T19:23:01Z","body":"Rebased to use @ajreckof's version.\r\n\r\nAnd added a test covering his `menu__debug` case, using existing files in the test dataset: searching for `colo.tres` used to prefer the shorter `./menu/ui_[colo]rs[.tres]` and now prefers `./menu/menu/characters/[colo]r[.tres]`.\r\n\r\nThe latest version also fixes `_is_word_boundary()` which incorrectly used `.size()` instead of `.length()` to check the length of a string.  Verified with a new test that failed under the old code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4246551249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4249859600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4249859600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4249859600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79T7YQ","user":{"login":"torcado194","id":9218934,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMTg5MzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9218934?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194","html_url":"https://github.com/torcado194","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torcado194/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T06:42:06Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T06:55:46Z","body":"Tested locally, works great. Fixes the main source of frustration I've had with the fuzzy search with my projects. Thank you so much!\r\n\r\nBefore and after:\r\n<img width=\"1564\" height=\"682\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83e048ce-657d-48a7-a4c2-6778efc71b3b\" />\r\n\r\nPerhaps this isn't a fit for this PR, but the last piece missing to cover my ideal fuzzy search result is sorting by filename length before full path length.\r\ne.g.\r\n```diff\r\n        struct FuzzySearchResultComparator {\r\n                bool operator()(const FuzzySearchResult &p_lhs, const FuzzySearchResult &p_rhs) const {\r\n-                       // Sort on (score, length, alphanumeric) to ensure consistent ordering.\r\n+                       // Sort on (score, filename length, path length, alphanumeric) to ensure consistent ordering.\r\n                        if (p_lhs.score == p_rhs.score) {\r\n-                               if (p_lhs.target.length() == p_rhs.target.length()) {\r\n+                               if (p_lhs.target.length() - p_lhs.dir_index ==  p_rhs.target.length() - p_rhs.dir_index) {\r\n+                                       if (p_lhs.target.length() == p_rhs.target.length()) {\r\n+                                               return p_lhs.target < p_rhs.target;\r\n+                                       }\r\n+                                       return p_lhs.target.length() < p_rhs.target.length();\r\n                                }\r\n-                               return p_lhs.target.length() < p_rhs.target.length();\r\n+                               return p_lhs.target.length() - p_lhs.dir_index < p_rhs.target.length() - p_rhs.dir_index;\r\n                        }\r\n                        return p_lhs.score > p_rhs.score;\r\n                }\r\n```\r\n\r\nResulting in:  \r\n<img width=\"782\" height=\"682\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5bd88579-1201-47e1-86fa-12b6da2d8341\" />\r\n\r\nNote that `../player.gd` and `../player.tscn` now show before `../player_action.gd`\r\nNot only is this more useful (to me), but it also matches my expectations from the UI putting much larger emphasis on the filename vs. the path.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4249859600/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4250319999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4250319999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4250319999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79Vrx_","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T08:10:01Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T08:10:01Z","body":"CC @a-johnston @samsface who worked on the last major refactor of the fuzzy matching algorithm in #98278.\r\nI've stopped counting how many times this algorithm has been tweaked, there often tends to be people happy or unhappy whatever we do. I tend to agree in general that a higher scoring for exact matching for the filename and start of the filename especially sound sensible to me.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4250319999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4251262789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4251262789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4251262789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79ZR9F","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T10:31:03Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T10:31:03Z","body":"I tested the current code, this PR, and @torcado194's patch on the project I used for the old pr and they all performed pretty similarly and predictably for me. I agree with the intuitions for the score changes, and seeing the filenames/structure in the screenshots it makes sense why they would be preferable. Since I only had my own project to index heuristics on, and was warned about the can of worms that was fuzzy search, I'm a bit surprised it hasn't already been tweaked/removed again :P\r\n\r\nRe. the scoring system, I looked over the code completion logic and functionally I think the element-wise score comparison is pretty similar to having different magnitudes of score contributions. The two algos do search and generate their subsequences differently, although the code completion logic was somewhat involved and I was just scanning. I think ideally the two could share logic but they are currently tuned for different tasks and I'd expect for most projects that there are more and longer filepaths compared to possible symbols, so something that works well for symbol search might be accurate but less responsive for file search. The path-aware fuzzy search code does work for non-paths since the filename bonus is applied uniformly for results, and the new heuristic this PR adds actually matches an existing code completion one `charac.push_back((matches[0].first == 0) ? 0 : 1);`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4251262789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4253980400","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117983#issuecomment-4253980400","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117983","id":4253980400,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79jpbw","user":{"login":"michaelgundlach","id":5141333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDEzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5141333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelgundlach","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelgundlach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-15T17:06:14Z","updated_at":"2026-04-15T17:06:14Z","body":"> I've stopped counting how many times this algorithm has been tweaked, there often tends to be people happy or unhappy whatever we do. I tend to agree in general that a higher scoring for exact matching for the filename and start of the filename especially sound sensible to me.\r\n\r\nI've tried to keep the scope of my change tiny so it strictly improves the algorithm, with minimal chance of making users unhappy.  I agree with @akien-mga, I'm hesitant to add in sorting by filename length, because some people won't like the new order.\r\n\r\nCould we maybe merge the code as it stands, then open a separate discussion / PR for other ideas in this thread (filename length sort, token word boundary detection, merging with code completion logic)?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4253980400/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"